<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct  sales of paper and five repurchase agreements whereby it had sought  to drain 3.378 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday,  dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>	AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	150 million    363 days   20.73 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    181 days   20.64 pct</p>
<p>	150 million     90 days   19.35 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed  as follows:</p>
<p>	500 million     42 days   21.00 pct</p>
<p>	600 million     41 days   20.79 pct</p>
<p>	600 million     28 days   20.87 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     20 days   21.14 pct</p>
<p>	228 million	3 days   23.89 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
